{:edb/db-before-t 2405 :edb/db-after-t 2406 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535718 50 #inst "2026-10-09T05:51:51.569Z" 13194139535718 true] [17592186124369 1020 #edb/ref 17592186363055 13194139535718 true] [17592186124531 1020 #edb/ref 17592186363048 13194139535718 true] [17592186124531 1020 #edb/ref 17592186363062 13194139535718 true] [17592186124531 1020 #edb/ref 17592186363069 13194139535718 true] [17592186363048 1017 #edb/ref 17592186363049 13194139535718 true] [17592186363048 1089 "q-129654" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363048 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535718 true] [17592186363048 1100 "Suppose that $f(x,y,z)$ is a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\nf(1,0,-1)=1,\\,{f}_{x}(1,0,-1)=-1,\\,{f}_{y}(1,0,-1)=-1,\\,{f}_{z}(1,0,-1)=0.\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,0,-1)$ estimate the value of $f(1.02,0.1,-0.96)$" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363048 1113 #uuid "e2824792-4fee-5f3f-be81-2e4b2980e7af" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363048 1145 "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,0,-1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(1,0,-1)+∇f(1,0,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-0,z-(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =f(1,0,-1)+⟨{f}_{x}(1,0,-1),{f}_{y}(1,0,-1),{f}_{z}(1,0,-1)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y,z+1⟩ \\\\  & =1+⟨-1,-1,0⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y,z+1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(1.02,0.1,-0.96)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=1.02,$ $y=0.1,$ and $z=-0.96$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.02,0.1,-0.96) & ≈1+⟨-1,-1,0⟩\\cdot ⟨1.02-1,0.1,-0.96+1⟩ \\\\  & =1+⟨-1,-1,0⟩\\cdot ⟨0.02,0.1,0.04⟩ \\\\  & =1-1(0.02)-1(0.1)+0(0.04) \\\\  & =1-0.02-0.1+0 \\\\  & =0.88\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363049 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363050 13194139535718 true] [17592186363049 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363051 13194139535718 true] [17592186363049 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363052 13194139535718 true] [17592186363049 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363053 13194139535718 true] [17592186363049 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363054 13194139535718 true] [17592186363049 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535718 true] [17592186363049 1041 "selection" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363049 1104 #edb/ref 17592186363051 13194139535718 true] [17592186363049 1110 #uuid "bfb73485-902b-5d18-b9b9-048f28380e6a" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363050 1034 "1.03" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363050 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535718 true] [17592186363050 1111 #uuid "5e056001-1d92-5766-8006-b42dc59e54d6" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363051 1034 "0.88" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363051 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535718 true] [17592186363051 1111 #uuid "500899d9-3be0-5e5a-911c-4af664d0adcf" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363052 1034 "0.98" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363052 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535718 true] [17592186363052 1111 #uuid "5ad6384f-5c57-5f5b-8dad-fc88c4721a3b" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363053 1034 "1.09" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363053 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535718 true] [17592186363053 1111 #uuid "a407e943-1fcb-56c2-8166-77dc98c90d48" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363054 1034 "0.93" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363054 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535718 true] [17592186363054 1111 #uuid "0082ecdf-47e5-53a5-895e-7a4e03248e03" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363055 1017 #edb/ref 17592186363056 13194139535718 true] [17592186363055 1089 "q-129746" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363055 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535718 true] [17592186363055 1100 "Let $f(x,y,z)=yz-x.$ Find the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(0,-1,1).$" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363055 1113 #uuid "9fed137c-3970-57b9-8c2b-495f775fd2ec" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363055 1145 "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(0,-1,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(0,-1,1)+∇f(0,-1,1)\\cdot ⟨x,y+1,z-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of $f,$ we have that $f(0,-1,1)=-1.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x} & =-1\\,⇒\\,{f}_{x}(0,-1,1)=-1, \\\\ {f}_{y} & =z\\,⇒\\,{f}_{y}(0,-1,1)=1, \\\\ {f}_{z} & =y\\,⇒\\,{f}_{z}(0,-1,1)=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient of the function at the point $(0,-1,1)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(0,-1,1) & =⟨{f}_{x}(0,-1,1),{f}_{y}(0,-1,1),{f}_{z}(0,-1,1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the linear approximation of the function $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(0,-1,1)+∇f(0,-1,1)\\cdot ⟨x,y+1,z-1⟩ \\\\  & ≈-1+⟨-1,1,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x,y+1,z-1⟩ \\\\  & ≈-1-(x)+(y+1)-(z-1) \\\\  & ≈1-x+y-z.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363057 13194139535718 true] [17592186363056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363058 13194139535718 true] [17592186363056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363059 13194139535718 true] [17592186363056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363060 13194139535718 true] [17592186363056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363061 13194139535718 true] [17592186363056 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535718 true] [17592186363056 1041 "selection" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363056 1104 #edb/ref 17592186363059 13194139535718 true] [17592186363056 1110 #uuid "d2e319fa-8986-5bcf-b645-e666599902b9" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363057 1034 "f(x,y,z)≈-3+2x-y+z" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363057 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535718 true] [17592186363057 1111 #uuid "7dd416d0-1ef2-51a8-93a4-3be0957eeb24" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363058 1034 "f(x,y,z)≈2x+y" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363058 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535718 true] [17592186363058 1111 #uuid "9433909f-0111-5198-840d-ad8d8b2b1180" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363059 1034 "f(x,y,z)≈1-x+y-z" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363059 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535718 true] [17592186363059 1111 #uuid "3b318543-6d6b-5b8b-9bf4-82ed13590598" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363060 1034 "f(x,y,z)≈-2+2y+3z" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363060 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535718 true] [17592186363060 1111 #uuid "dd3de839-b10f-5875-85e0-f384a2825ab4" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363061 1034 "f(x,y,z)≈-x-y-2z" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363061 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535718 true] [17592186363061 1111 #uuid "b36d70c2-de52-5d60-94b9-f3ac92184afb" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363062 1017 #edb/ref 17592186363063 13194139535718 true] [17592186363062 1089 "q-98342" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363062 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535718 true] [17592186363062 1100 "Suppose that $f(x,y,z)$ is a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\nf(1,2,3)=3,\\,{f}_{x}(1,2,3)=-2,\\,{f}_{y}(1,2,3)=1,\\,{f}_{z}(1,2,3)=3.\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,2,3)$ estimate the value of $f(0.96,1.98,3.03).$" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363062 1113 #uuid "164023df-d37c-516f-9c3b-868f9fb8729b" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363062 1145 "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,2,3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(1,2,3)+∇f(1,2,3)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-2,z-3⟩ \\\\  & =f(1,2,3)+⟨{f}_{x}(1,2,3),{f}_{y}(1,2,3),{f}_{z}(1,2,3)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-2,z-3⟩ \\\\  & =3+⟨-2,1,3⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-2,z-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(0.96,1.98,3.03)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=0.96,$ $y=1.98,$ and $z=3.03$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.96,1.98,3.03) & ≈3+⟨-2,1,3⟩\\cdot ⟨0.96-1,1.98-2,3.03-3⟩ \\\\  & =3+⟨-2,1,3⟩\\cdot ⟨-0.04,-0.02,0.03⟩ \\\\  & =3+0.08-0.02+0.09 \\\\  & =3.15\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363063 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363064 13194139535718 true] [17592186363063 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363065 13194139535718 true] [17592186363063 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363066 13194139535718 true] [17592186363063 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363067 13194139535718 true] [17592186363063 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363068 13194139535718 true] [17592186363063 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535718 true] [17592186363063 1041 "selection" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363063 1104 #edb/ref 17592186363064 13194139535718 true] [17592186363063 1110 #uuid "0e5ed355-6a4f-5c4a-8d01-a99e4ac83ef1" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363064 1034 "3.15" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363064 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535718 true] [17592186363064 1111 #uuid "738ed73d-b486-521e-ad84-9e1de1647447" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363065 1034 "3.03" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363065 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535718 true] [17592186363065 1111 #uuid "cfa07642-7da2-524c-b6b8-94ba1ac508af" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363066 1034 "3.01" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363066 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535718 true] [17592186363066 1111 #uuid "24be30f9-d8d7-5da8-bf5a-75c0a7cd1df8" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363067 1034 "2.99" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363067 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535718 true] [17592186363067 1111 #uuid "c2cc5401-76ab-5776-a2e9-af41f884cc7d" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363068 1034 "3.25" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363068 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535718 true] [17592186363068 1111 #uuid "a9ae433e-248f-5100-a081-dfb1ef3fe8ac" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363069 1017 #edb/ref 17592186363070 13194139535718 true] [17592186363069 1089 "q-98347" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363069 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535718 true] [17592186363069 1100 "Let $f(x,y,z)$ be a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & f(3,0,4)=25, &  & {f}_{x}(x,y,z)=\\frac{5x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}, \\\\  & {f}_{y}(x,y,z)=\\frac{5y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}, &  & {f}_{z}(x,y,z)=\\frac{5z}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(3,0,4),$ estimate the value of $f(3.01,0.1,3.99).$" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363069 1113 #uuid "a6fb78aa-f2e7-500d-a880-3c8ff234bc2f" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363069 1145 "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(3,0,4)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(3,0,4)+∇f(3,0,4)\\cdot ⟨x-3,y-0,z-4⟩ \\\\  & =25+⟨{f}_{x}(3,0,4),{f}_{y}(3,0,4),{f}_{z}(3,0,4)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,y,z-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{x}(3,0,4)$, ${f}_{y}(3,0,4)$ and ${f}_{z}(3,0,4),$ using the given partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(3,0,4) & =\\frac{5(3)}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}}}=3 \\\\ {f}_{y}(3,0,4) & =\\frac{5(0)}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}}}=0 \\\\ {f}_{z}(3,0,4) & =\\frac{5(4)}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}}}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈25+⟨3,0,4⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,y,z-4⟩.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can estimate $f(3.01,0.1,3.99)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=3.01,y=0.1$ and $z=3.99,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3.01,0.1,3.99) & ≈25+⟨3,0,4⟩\\cdot ⟨3.01-3,0.1,3.99-4⟩ \\\\  & =25+⟨3,0,4⟩\\cdot ⟨0.01,0.1,-0.01⟩ \\\\  & =25+0.03-0.04 \\\\  & =24.99\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363070 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363071 13194139535718 true] [17592186363070 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363072 13194139535718 true] [17592186363070 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363073 13194139535718 true] [17592186363070 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363074 13194139535718 true] [17592186363070 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363075 13194139535718 true] [17592186363070 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535718 true] [17592186363070 1041 "selection" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363070 1104 #edb/ref 17592186363075 13194139535718 true] [17592186363070 1110 #uuid "5a967a5f-c3be-5a15-b50f-2bcf02c1822c" 13194139535718 true] [17592186363071 1034 "